+<section id="github-update-20261030" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">30 October: evidence assessment, uploads and authorization research</h2><p>VAP PR #30 proposes evidence bindings; #31 provides an offline assessor (20 test methods; 23/23 matching scenarios); #32 exercises loopback uploads (39 methods; 17/17 upload cases and 17/17 evidence rechecks match). Evidect #20 adds a synthetic authorization gate (37 tests; 18 scenarios); #21 adds optional SQLite replay reservations (33 new tests; 70 gate-specific tests and four process scenarios). Counts remain separate by scope.</p><p>All results are first-party CI checks. Upload case UL-14 shows a <strong>successful bypass outside the gate</strong>, not OS isolation or production bypass prevention. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 159 / 26 and 306 / 140 test records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-30-incident-evidence-authorization-research-update/">Read the five updates and limits →</a></p></section>
 <section id="github-update-20261029" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">VSO updates SDK evidence checks, the Explorer demo and Evidect reproduction guidance</h2><p>29 October: stricter SDK inputs, an API-connected signed-evidence Explorer route and Evidect reproduction guidance are available. The legacy dashboard and historical 159 / 26 and 306 / 140 test records remain separate. Experimental extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>.</p><p>The new demo uses signed synthetic evidence; intact full evidence is still INDETERMINATE. The API-disconnected / unsigned description in the 27 October record applies to the legacy dashboard.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-29-sdk-evidence-demo-reproduction-update/">Read the update and limits →</a> · <a href="https://veritaschain.org/explorer/app/#/evidence-demo">SDK Evidence Demo</a> · <a href="https://evidect.veritaschain.org/methodology/#reproduce">Evidect</a></p></section>
 <section id="github-update-20261028" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">VSO updates VAP-LAP references, VAP errata and SDK boundary checks</h2><p>28 October: VAP-LAP proposal links, current Draft 3 errata/hash references and SDK boundary checks are available. SDK first-party CI passed <strong>306 Python and 140 TypeScript tests per matrix job</strong>, including 13 shared cases and 15 focused tests per language. The Explorer 159-test notice below is retained separately. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction has <strong>not been established</strong>.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-28-vap-lap-sdk-status-update/">Read the update and limits →</a></p></section>
 <section id="explorer-update-20261027" class="status" aria-label="Explorer update — 27 October 2026"><h2 style="margin-top:0">27 October: Explorer API's 159 tests and public GUI update</h2><p>The separate Explorer API fixed search-filter validation and exact nanosecond time-range comparisons. Its first-party CI passed <strong>159 tests</strong>, with zero failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs. This is a repository/CI checkpoint, not confirmation of a production API deployment.</p><p>The <a href="https://veritaschain.org/explorer/app/">public Explorer GUI</a> now requires an explicit tree size for its inclusion calculation, handles uneven branches and rejects malformed proofs. The GUI's separate first-party suite passed <strong>26 tests</strong>. The public page remains an API-disconnected demo with 12 synthetic leaves: unsigned, externally unanchored, and not hashes derived from the displayed event contents. A path matching a supplied root does not authenticate the root or tree size, or verify event contents, signatures or external anchors.</p><p>First-party publication checks exercised the 12 demo inclusion controls, notice placement at seven widths, and mobile controls. These checks are separate from the 159 API tests and <strong>do not establish independent reproduction</strong>. VAP's historical teaching snippets and the fixed RTA review target remain separate. VAP is still Draft 3; experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain <strong>unadopted</strong>, and independent third-party reproduction has <strong>not been established</strong>.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-report-intake-explorer-update/#explorer-update-20261027">Detailed update and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-explorer-api/actions/runs/40355875498">API CI: 159 tests</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-explorer-gui/actions/runs/40360033313">GUI CI: 26 tests</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-site