 <section id="github-update-20261028" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">VSO updates VAP-LAP references, VAP errata and SDK boundary checks</h2><p>28 October: VAP-LAP proposal links, current Draft 3 errata/hash references and SDK boundary checks are available. SDK first-party CI passed <strong>306 Python and 140 TypeScript tests per matrix job</strong>, including 13 shared cases and 15 focused tests per language. The Explorer 159-test notice below is retained separately. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction has <strong>not been established</strong>.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-28-vap-lap-sdk-status-update/">Read the update and limits →</a></p></section>
 <aside class="status" aria-label="GitHub and status update"><strong>GitHub and status update — 26 October 2026</strong><p><strong>RTA verifier review checkpoint:</strong> the separate VCP RTA repository now provides fixes and a fixed review target (<code>cc695fe</code>). Recorded first-party CI passed 809 regression and 15 separate historical tests per environment, while the 40-event evidence replay remains <strong>INDETERMINATE</strong>. This does not establish independent reproduction, full conformance or a new release. <a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-rta-verifier-checkpoint/">Read the RTA update and limits →</a> A <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/actions/runs/40263948191">separate first-party CI</a> also completed the unchanged published recipe from a fresh network clone through final assessment on Python 3.11 and 3.13.5; this is procedure validation, not independent reproduction.</p><p>The <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-spec/pull/16">VCP candidate schema and synthetic checker</a> and <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/pull/26">VAP three-valued verification proposal</a> have been incorporated as research. Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain <strong>unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established</strong>. VAP v1.2.0 is still Draft 3. VCP v1.2 is Released, with known integrity issues under review and full conformance to VAP unestablished. This website's code examples are not a native VCP conformance verifier.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-sdk/releases/tag/v0.1.0">vcp-sdk v0.1.0</a> is a first-party pre-release offline core on GitHub, not a PyPI/npm release, an implementation of vcp-sdk-spec, or an independent external implementation. Its interpretation choices do not adopt normative changes.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/blob/81fa81e01ef9418c3fb7a02ddfc7fd72d993b6b1/README.md#implementation-status-mandatory-disclosure">VSO's published disclosure as of 25 October 2026</a> reports zero external implementations and zero Evidence Packs accepted in proceedings. These are disclosed project counts, not an independent assessment. <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/blob/81fa81e01ef9418c3fb7a02ddfc7fd72d993b6b1/disclosures/2026-10-24-commercial-contracts.md">Earlier commercial figures remain withdrawn pending verification</a>; this is not a zero-contract finding. Current normative requirements, existing implementations, signed data, fixed distributions and K3 are unchanged by this website update.</p><p><a class="btn" href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-vcp-research-update/">Read the research update and evidence →</a></p></aside>
